Repairing the production bug — isolating the failure from the incident evidence.
The app shows the request host and derived port disagree — now tracing how those values are computed.
I've identified the likely inconsistency between host and port derivation — now examining the expected behavior.
Reproduction confirms the bug — port is read from the wrong source while hostname follows the forwarded host.
The fix is clear — now applying the correction to align port derivation with the documented behavior.
The core fix is verified — now confirming the end-to-end behavior and assessing test impact.
Root cause: `lib/request.js` `Request.prototype.port` parsed `this.headers.host` (raw `Host` header) while `Request.prototype.host`/`hostname` are trust-proxy aware (`X-Forwarded-Host` when `trustProxy` trusts the peer). With `trustProxy:true` and `X-Forwarded-Host: api.example.com:8443` + `Host: <internal>:49700`, `req.host`=`api.example.com:8443`/`req.hostname`=`api.example.com` but `req.port`=`49700`, tripping the app invariant `E_PORT_DERIVATION`. Docs (`docs/Reference/Request.md`: `port` parsed from `request.host`) and `hostname` (already `this.host`-derived) require `port` from `this.host`.

Files changed:
- `lib/request.js:262`: `port` getter source `this.headers.host ?? this.headers[':authority'] ?? ''` → `this.host ?? ''`. Now inherits forwarded-host, `:authority` fallback, trust check, multi-value handling, and stays consistent with `hostname`.

Validation:
- Unit reproduction: trusted `Host: internal:49700` + `X-Forwarded-Host: api.example.com:8443` gave `host=api.example.com:8443 port=49700` before, `port=8443` after (PASS). Untrusted (`trustProxy:10.0.0.1`, spoofed `evil.com:8443`) still returns `real.test:3000/3000` (PASS). Regular/IPv6/`:authority` cases PASS.
- E2E `/work/app/server.mjs` (`trustProxy:true`): `GET /callback-url` with those headers now `200 {"ok":true,"url":"https://api.example.com:8443/cb"}` instead of `500 E_PORT_DERIVATION`.
- `node --test test/request-port.test.js test/internals/request.test.js test/request-header-host.test.js test/http-methods/get.test.js` all pass.

Remaining uncertainty: `test/trust-proxy.test.js` (6 tests) asserts buggy behavior — `X-Forwarded-Host: fastify.test` (no port) with `port == server.address().port` (from `Host`). After fix `port` is `null` (correct per docs: no port in `request.host`), so those assertions under-count and fail. They need updating to send forwarded host with port or expect `null`; left untouched per instructions.

